@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `usca-holidays`
IMPORT `usca-general-provisions`
IMPORT `usca-operation-of-statutes`
IMPORT `usca-deputies`
IMPORT `usca-further-limbs`
IMPORT `usca-canons-of-reading`
IMPORT `usca-remedies-and-actions`
IMPORT `usca-definitions`
IMPORT `usca-proclaimed-days`
IMPORT `usca-assessed-value`

-- Independent tests.  Expected values come from ANSWERS.md, written from the source text before any .l4 file was opened.
-- "S<n>" is the scenario number in ANSWERS.md.  "Not covered" in the encoding's own convention is #ASSERT REFUSED.
-- Helpers below only fix an argument (a calendar, a clock reading); they carry no expected value.

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`gov calendar` d MEANS `a holiday under Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for the state` `no day is supplied` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`civ calendar` d MEANS `a holiday under Civ. Code § 7` `no day is supplied` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`civ business day` d MEANS `a business day under Civ. Code § 9` `no day is supplied` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ccp 12 calendar` d MEANS `a holiday for computing time under Code Civ. Proc. § 12` `no day is supplied` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ccp 12a calendar with sundays` d MEANS `a holiday for the extension of Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), taking in the Sundays of § 10` `no day is supplied` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`gov business day` d MEANS NOT (`gov calendar` d)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Moment
`the moment on` d `at second` s MEANS Moment WITH `the day` IS d, `seconds after midnight` IS s

GIVEN appointed IS A LIST OF DATE
      thanksgiving IS A LIST OF DATE
      goodFriday IS A LIST OF DATE
      closed IS A LIST OF DATE
      bankClosings IS A LIST OF DATE
      lny IS A LIST OF DATE
      diwali IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Days supplied by the caller`
`the days supplied are` appointed thanksgiving goodFriday closed bankClosings lny diwali MEANS
    `Days supplied by the caller` WITH
        `Lunar New Year days` IS lny
        `Diwali days` IS diwali
        `days appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving or holiday` IS appointed
        `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day` IS thanksgiving
        `Good Friday days` IS goodFriday
        `days on which March 31 is observed instead` IS EMPTY
        `March 31 itself stays a holiday in a year in which it is observed on another day` IS TRUE
        `judicial holidays specified in Code Civ. Proc. section 135` IS EMPTY
        `days a public office is closed for the whole day` IS closed
        `bank closings under the Bank Extraordinary Situation Closing Act` IS bankClosings

